      "id": 1,
      "text": "Marietta sits at the outlet of Otisco Lake, where Nine Mile Creek begins its northward journey.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marietta%2C_New_York",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1869 a dam at Otisco Lake’s outlet raised the water level nine feet to create a reservoir for the Erie Canal.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marietta%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Marcellus & Otisco Lake Railway, opened in 1905, stretched 9 miles with 46 curves through Marietta’s valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marietta%2C_New_York",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By the mid‑19th century, Marietta had grown into a small milling and commercial hub near the lake outlet.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marietta%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1985 the Onondaga County Water Authority completed a multi‑million‑dollar filtration plant near Otisco Lake, delivering water by gravity to Marcellus.",
